{
  "slug": "hats",
  "name": "Hats",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Your personal AI dev team. Five specialized roles — Manager, Designer, CTO, QA, and Developer — each with isolated context and permissions.\n\nThe Manager writes Gherkin specs, then each role takes over: Designer creates mockups, CTO picks the stack, QA writes tests from requirements (not implementation), and Developer builds the code.\n\nRole separation prevents shared blind spots — the QA can't see Developer instructions and vice versa.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **10 skills**, **5 agents** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (10): `autopilot` (Run the QA ↔ Developer loop autonomously until tests pass), `cto` (Switch to the CTO role), `designer` (Switch to the Designer role), `developer` (Switch to the Developer role), `doctor` (Diagnose and fix a Hats project structure (missing dirs, symlinks, files)), `init` (Initialize Hats in a new or existing project), `manager` (Switch to the Manager role), `qa` (Switch to the QA role), and 2 more\n- **Agents** (5): `cto` (CTO), `designer` (Designer), `developer` (Developer), `manager` (Technical Manager), `qa` (QA Engineer)\n- **Hooks** (1): `PreToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install hats@claude-community` from `deadsimple-xyz/hats`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 10,
    "agent": 5,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "deadsimple"
  },
